===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*dʰeyǵʰ-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|figure}}, borrowed from {{der|en|fro|figure}}, from {{der|en|la|figūra||form, shape, form of a word, a figure of speech, {{cog|la-lat|-}} a sketch, drawing}}, from {{m|la|fingō||to form, shape, mold, fashion}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*dʰeyǵʰ-||to mold, shape, form, knead}}. Cognate with {{cog|grc|τεῖχος}}, {{cog|sa|देग्धि|tr=dégdhi}}, {{cog|ang|dāg||dough}}. More at {{l|en|dough}}. {{doublet|en|figura}}.

